WEBVTT

00:16:00.371 --> 00:16:01.662
And all of those you know,

00:16:01.662 --> 00:16:04.996
there's those little changes and
adjustments that we make.

00:16:05.746 --> 00:16:08.579
We could think about them as experiments
and then we could say, OK, well,

00:16:08.787 --> 00:16:10.746
you know what what information
what data do

00:16:10.746 --> 00:16:13.912
I need in order to find out if that was
a successful or failed experiment?

00:16:14.621 --> 00:16:16.621
And I I think that's a huge step.

00:16:16.621 --> 00:16:20.662
And I guess the other thing I would I
would just put on the table is when

00:16:20.662 --> 00:16:21.621
I was writing the book again,

00:16:21.621 --> 00:16:25.454
I made a list of all the things that I
know I'm completely ignorant about.

00:16:26.371 --> 00:16:29.662
And my goal was was actually
not to reduce the list,

00:16:29.662 --> 00:16:31.704
it was to expand the list. Mm hmm.